WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.086
The world of Dune is known for its scale

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:06.715
and its futuristic yet
strangely familiar technology,

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:11.261
But its most recognizable feature
is probably its brutal environment.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:15.390
According to research, humans can survive for only about 10 minutes

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:18.852
at a temperature of 121 degrees Celsius.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.770
If they're in a dry environment

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.898
and 60 degrees Celsius
if they're in a humid environment.

00:00:24.107 --> 00:00:28.236
But the people of the planet
Arrakis have figured out a way to survive

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:33.491
in a climate that's on average
between 45 degrees Celsius in the lowlands

00:00:33.491 --> 00:00:38.204
and 70 degrees Celsius in the waistlines
And it's not just the heat.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:43.043
They have to deal with the wind,
which blows up to 750 kilometers an hour.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:46.671
The sandstorms
and a complete lack of water.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.925
and not only survive,
they've built cities and wealth

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:56.514
and also some
really strange local customs.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:57.474
And the world is

00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:01.686
full of these details,
both high-tech and low-tech, that exhibit

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:05.982
how they've managed to survive
in these brutal, inhospitable conditions.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:10.028
And although it's set in the year
10,000, this fictional world

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:13.698
might actually give us some insights
into our own futures as well.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:19.204
A portion of this video is sponsored
by Wayfair,

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:20.330
Frank Herbert

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.501
wrote Dune in 1965
after his visit to the Oregon Dunes.

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:28.046
This was a time when he was kind
of struggling with his career.

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:33.093
He went to Florence, Oregon, to write
a magazine article about these sandstorms.

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:36.596
Apparently, winds were blowing
in from the Pacific Ocean

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.225
and destabilizing the sand,
and it was threatening the communities

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:41.351
along the coast.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:45.105
But instead of writing the article,
he ended up writing

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.357
a bestselling masterpiece.

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:51.277
Oh, and he was
really into magic mushrooms.

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:55.156
No big deal.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.493
Arrakis, as you might have
guessed, was written to be allegorical

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:01.704
to the petrol-rich countries
like the ones in the Middle East.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.708
And if you don't know the story,
the reason why they stay living in this

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:10.338
inhospitable planet is because it's
the only place in the universe

00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:14.217
they can produce Spice,
also known as Mélange.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.096
Spice is a fictional substance
that can extend life.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.057
It can give you enhanced abilities.

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:24.936
And you can only do space travel
If you're high on spice

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:29.274
And therefore, it's the most valuable
substance in the universe.

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:33.194
as a byproduct of a sandworms lifecycle,
which is intertwined

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:34.988
with the desert ecology of the planet.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:38.992
And so as the producer
of the most valuable substance

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:42.871
in the universe,
It makes Arrakis the only source of spice,

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:47.709
the wealthiest and most strategically
important location in the universe.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:50.587
There have been efforts
to terraform the planet to be

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:53.756
a little bit more livable,
but changing the atmosphere

00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:57.760
will essentially deprive
the planet of its most valuable resource.

00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:01.014
So all of these efforts
have been stalled So,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:05.894
yes, it's a story about sandworms
and space travel, but it's also about

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:09.272
geopolitical conflicts
around the exploitation

00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:15.570
of natural resources
and the effects of a changing climate.

00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:17.155
Arrakis sits on a sheet of

00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:21.326
bedrock nestled within a mountain
bore on the north pole of the planet.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:24.746
And these nice people actually made
a climate simulation of the planet

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:28.249
Arrakis to see how accurate
the descriptions in the book were.

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:29.209
In the book,

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:34.047
it describes a planet with unforgiving sun
and wasteland of sand and rock.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:38.635
But as you move closer to the polar
regions toward the cities of Arrakeen,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:42.597
it starts to change into something
that might be a little bit more livable.

00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:47.852
But actually, in their simulation,
they found the opposite.

00:03:48.019 --> 00:03:51.981
The overall climate of the planet
is actually relatively mild

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:56.152
and the warmest months in the tropics
hit around 45 degrees Celsius.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:59.572
And the coldest dropped
just below 15 degrees Celsius.

00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:03.660
But when you get into the polar regions,
that's when you get the extreme

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.827
temperatures.

00:04:04.827 --> 00:04:08.414
Summers can get as hot as 70 degrees
Celsius and as low

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:17.507
as -75 degrees
in the winters But I digress,

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.299
There's not a

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:22.220
whole lot of information
on how the city is built or laid out.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:27.267
But what we do know is that the city of
or Arrakeen is nestled within a mountain wall

00:04:27.475 --> 00:04:31.521
which gives them protection from the sun
and the wind and the sandworms.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:35.858
They've also built in a shield wall
