They essentially capture wind
and direct it into buildings

00:15:54.578 --> 00:15:57.539
to provide natural ventilation
and passive cooling.

00:15:57.539 --> 00:16:01.961
The tower is designed to catch the wind
and funnel it downward

00:16:02.211 --> 00:16:05.881
and the pressure differential pushes
hot air out of the building.

00:16:05.923 --> 00:16:08.926
Sometimes they're paired
with an underground channel transporting

00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:13.305
water called canards, which cooled the air
before it circulates the building.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:14.974
There's even modern buildings.

00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:18.102
Let's use wind captures
with some really great results.

00:16:18.185 --> 00:16:21.522
and it's allowed them to avoid mechanical
AC units and also

00:16:21.522 --> 00:16:25.275
reduce their emissions.

00:16:25.359 --> 00:16:28.654
the most interesting part of Dune for me
is this huge

00:16:28.654 --> 00:16:32.366
contrast between the local Fremen
and the ruling families.

